@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `usca-interpretation-time`

-- California holidays, as predicates other encodings can pass to usca-interpretation-time.
--
-- Sources: Gov. Code §§ 6700-6705, Civ. Code §§ 7, 7.1, 9, Code Civ. Proc. §§ 10, 12, 12a, 12b.  The quotation lines are copied
-- by script from the converter-made plain-text rendering of the sections (not the official text) and checked against it.
--
-- Gov. Code § 6700(a) names some days by the calendar (the third Monday in January, July 4) and some the text leaves
-- to be supplied: the date of Lunar New Year and of Diwali, Good Friday, days appointed by the President or Governor.
-- Code Civ. Proc. § 135, which §§ 10 and 12a point to for the judicial holidays, is not in the deposited text, so
-- its days are an input too.  Nothing here computes a date the text does not give a rule for.
-- Target: unstable.  Imports: prelude, daydate and usca-interpretation-time.

§ `Days the text leaves to be supplied`

DECLARE `Days supplied by the caller` HAS
    `Lunar New Year days`                                                                  IS A LIST OF DATE
    `Diwali days`                                                                          IS A LIST OF DATE
    `days appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving or holiday` IS A LIST OF DATE
    `Thursdays appointed as Thanksgiving Day`                                              IS A LIST OF DATE
    `Good Friday days`                                                                     IS A LIST OF DATE
    `days on which March 31 is observed instead`                                           IS A LIST OF DATE
    `March 31 itself stays a holiday in a year in which it is observed on another day`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `judicial holidays specified in Code Civ. Proc. section 135`                           IS A LIST OF DATE
    `days a public office is closed for the whole day`                                     IS A LIST OF DATE
    `bank closings under the Bank Extraordinary Situation Closing Act`                     IS A LIST OF DATE

-- Nothing supplied.  Not a default of the text: it is the caller saying that it supplies no such day.
GIVETH A `Days supplied by the caller`
`no day is supplied` MEANS
    `Days supplied by the caller` WITH
        `Lunar New Year days` IS EMPTY
        `Diwali days` IS EMPTY
        `days appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving or holiday` IS EMPTY
        `Thursdays appointed as Thanksgiving Day` IS EMPTY
        `Good Friday days` IS EMPTY
        `days on which March 31 is observed instead` IS EMPTY
        `March 31 itself stays a holiday in a year in which it is observed on another day` IS TRUE
        `judicial holidays specified in Code Civ. Proc. section 135` IS EMPTY
        `days a public office is closed for the whole day` IS EMPTY
        `bank closings under the Bank Extraordinary Situation Closing Act` IS EMPTY

§ `Dates named by the calendar`

-- The n-th given weekday of a month, weekday 0 being Sunday as in daydate.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      weekday IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the n-th given weekday of a month` n weekday month year MEANS
    YMD year month 1 PLUS ((weekday MINUS `Weekday of` (YMD year month 1) PLUS 7) MODULO 7) PLUS (7 TIMES (n MINUS 1))

GIVEN weekday IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last given weekday of a month` weekday month year MEANS
    lastDay MINUS ((`Weekday of` lastDay MINUS weekday PLUS 7) MODULO 7)
    WHERE
        lastDay MEANS YMD year month (`Days in month` month year)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      month IS A NUMBER
      day IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the date is the given day of the given month` d month day MEANS
    DATE_MONTH d EQUALS month AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS day

§ `Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701: holidays in this state`

-- § 6700(a)(2), (5), (6), (8), (10)-(18): the days the text fixes by the calendar.  Left out, because each needs something the
-- text leaves to the caller or is limited to some bodies: (1) Sundays (see `is a Sunday`), (3) Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr.
-- Day, (4) Lunar New Year, (7) March 31, (9) Diwali, (19) Good Friday from noon until 3 p.m., (20) days appointed by the
-- President or Governor.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:8 | 6700. (a) The holidays in this state are:
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:9 | (1) Every Sunday.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:10 | (2) January 1.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:11 | (3) The third Monday in January, known as “Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr. Day.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:12 | (4) The date corresponding with the second new moon following the winter solstice, or the third new moon following the winter solstice should an intercalary month intervene, known as “Lunar New Year.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:13 | (5) February 12, known as “Lincoln Day.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:14 | (6) The third Monday in February.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:15 | (7) March 31, known as “Farmworkers Day.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:16 | (8) April 24, known as “Genocide Remembrance Day.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:17 | (9) The 15th day of the month of Kartik in the Hindu lunar calendar of each year, known as “Diwali.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:18 | (10) The last Monday in May.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:19 | (11) June 19, known as “Juneteenth.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:20 | (12) July 4.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:21 | (13) The first Monday in September.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:22 | (14) September 9, known as “Admission Day.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:23 | (15) The fourth Friday in September, known as “Native American Day.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:24 | (16) The second Monday in October, known as “Columbus Day.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:25 | (17) November 11, known as “Veterans Day.”
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:26 | (18) December 25.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:27 | (19) Good Friday from 12 noon until 3 p.m.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:28 | (20) (A) Every day appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving, or holiday.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:29 | (B) Except for the Thursday in November appointed as Thanksgiving Day, this paragraph and paragraphs (3), (4), and (7) shall not apply to a city, county, or district unless made applicable by charter, or by ordinance or resolution of the governing body
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:30 | thereof.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:31 | (b) If this section is in conflict with the provisions of a memorandum of understanding reached pursuant to Chapter 12 (commencing with Section 3560) of Division 4 of Title 1, the memorandum of understanding shall be controlling without further legislative action, except that if those provisions of a memorandum of understanding require the expenditure of funds, the provisions shall not become effective unless approved by the Legislature in the annual Budget Act.
@ref Gov. Code § 6700(a) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:8-31)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 6700(a) fixes the day by the calendar` d MEANS
        `the date is the given day of the given month` d 1 1
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 2 12
    OR  d EQUALS `the n-th given weekday of a month` 3 1 2 year
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 4 24
    OR  d EQUALS `the last given weekday of a month` 1 5 year
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 6 19
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 7 4
    OR  d EQUALS `the n-th given weekday of a month` 1 1 9 year
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 9 9
    OR  d EQUALS `the n-th given weekday of a month` 4 5 9 year
    OR  d EQUALS `the n-th given weekday of a month` 2 1 10 year
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 11 11
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 12 25
    WHERE
        year MEANS DATE_YEAR d

@ref Gov. Code § 6700(a)(3) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:8-31)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 6700(a)(3) makes the day a holiday` d MEANS
    d EQUALS `the n-th given weekday of a month` 3 1 1 (DATE_YEAR d)

-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:33 | 6701. (a) If January 1, February 12, March 31, July 4, September 9, November 11, or December 25 falls upon a Sunday, the Monday following is a holiday.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:34 | (b) If November
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:35 | 11 falls upon a Saturday, the preceding Friday is a holiday.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:36 | (c) If March 31 falls upon a Tuesday, Wednesday, or Thursday, the Legislature may observe the holiday on one of the following:
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:37 | (1) The preceding Friday.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:38 | (2) The preceding Monday.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:39 | (3) The following Friday.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:40 | (d) If
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:41 | any holiday designated in Section 6700 falls on a Saturday, the board of supervisors of any county may by ordinance or resolution provide that an alternate day shall be a holiday for the employees of the county, except those employees of the county working as court attachés.
@ref Gov. Code § 6701(a), (b) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:33-41)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`one of the days Gov. Code § 6701(a) names` d MEANS
        `the date is the given day of the given month` d 1 1
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 2 12
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 3 31
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 7 4
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 9 9
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 11 11
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 12 25

-- § 6701(a): a Monday following a Sunday that is one of those days.  (b): a Friday preceding a Saturday that is November 11.
@ref Gov. Code § 6701(a), (b) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:33-41)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 6701(a) or (b) makes the day a holiday` d MEANS
        (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 1 AND `one of the days Gov. Code § 6701(a) names` (d MINUS 1))
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 5 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d PLUS 1) 11 11)

-- § 6700(a)(7), § 6701(c): March 31, "Farmworkers Day".  When March 31 falls on a Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday "the Legislature
-- may observe the holiday on" another day.  The text does not say whether March 31 itself then stops being a holiday (fork
-- F-6701c in NOTES), so the caller says, and the observed day is one the caller supplies.
@ref Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), § 6701(c) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:8-31, src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:33-41)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` supplied d MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem d (supplied's `days on which March 31 is observed instead`) THEN TRUE
        IF `the date is the given day of the given month` d 3 31
            THEN (NOT observedThisYear) OR supplied's `March 31 itself stays a holiday in a year in which it is observed on another day`
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHERE
        observedThisYear MEANS any (GIVEN x YIELD DATE_YEAR x EQUALS DATE_YEAR d) (supplied's `days on which March 31 is observed instead`)

-- § 6700(a)(1)-(18), (20)(A) for the state: every day the text names or fixes, with the days left to the caller taken from `supplied`.
@ref Gov. Code § 6700(a), § 6701 (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:8-31, src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:33-41)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holiday under Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701 for the state` supplied d MEANS
        `is a Sunday` d
    OR  `Gov. Code § 6700(a) fixes the day by the calendar` d
    OR  `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(3) makes the day a holiday` d
    OR  `Gov. Code § 6701(a) or (b) makes the day a holiday` d
    OR  `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` supplied d
    OR  elem d (supplied's `Lunar New Year days`)
    OR  elem d (supplied's `Diwali days`)
    OR  elem d (supplied's `days appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving or holiday`)
    OR  elem d (supplied's `Thursdays appointed as Thanksgiving Day`)

-- § 6700(a)(20)(B): "Except for the Thursday in November appointed as Thanksgiving Day, this paragraph and paragraphs (3), (4), and
-- (7) shall not apply to a city, county, or district unless made applicable by charter, or by ordinance or resolution".
@ref Gov. Code § 6700(a)(20)(B) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:8-31)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holiday enumerated in Gov. Code § 6700 for a city, county or district` supplied `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` d MEANS
        `is a Sunday` d
    OR  `Gov. Code § 6700(a) fixes the day by the calendar` d
    OR  elem d (supplied's `Diwali days`)
    OR  elem d (supplied's `Thursdays appointed as Thanksgiving Day`)
    OR  (`paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` AND
            (    `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(3) makes the day a holiday` d
              OR `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(7), as § 6701(c) qualifies it, makes the day a holiday` supplied d
              OR elem d (supplied's `Lunar New Year days`)
              OR elem d (supplied's `days appointed by the President or Governor for a public fast, thanksgiving or holiday`)))

-- The same, with the Mondays and Fridays that § 6701(a) and (b) add.
@ref Gov. Code § 6700(a)(20)(B), § 6701(a), (b) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:8-31, src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:33-41)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holiday under Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701 for a city, county or district` supplied `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` d MEANS
        `a holiday enumerated in Gov. Code § 6700 for a city, county or district` supplied `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` d
    OR  `Gov. Code § 6701(a) or (b) makes the day a holiday` d

-- § 6701(d): "If any holiday designated in Section 6700 falls on a Saturday, the board of supervisors of any county may by ordinance or
-- resolution provide that an alternate day shall be a holiday for the employees of the county, except those employees of the county
-- working as court attaches."  The caller supplies the alternate days a board has provided.  The text says that the alternate day is a
-- holiday for those employees and does not say that the Saturday then stops being one, so nothing is taken away (fork F-6701d in NOTES).
@ref Gov. Code § 6701(d) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:33-41)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alternate days the board of supervisors has provided` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the employee works as a court attache` IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holiday for an employee of a county, taking in the alternate days of Gov. Code § 6701(d)` supplied `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` `the alternate days the board of supervisors has provided` `the employee works as a court attache` d MEANS
        `a holiday under Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701 for a city, county or district` supplied `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` d
    OR  ((NOT `the employee works as a court attache`) AND elem d `the alternate days the board of supervisors has provided`)

-- § 6700(a)(19): Good Friday "from 12 noon until 3 p.m.", a stretch of a day, so a function of the moment.  At noon the holiday has
-- begun; at 3 p.m. exactly the text does not say whether it has ended ("until"), so that instant is refused.
@ref Gov. Code § 6700(a)(19) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:8-31)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      m IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the moment falls in the Good Friday holiday of Gov. Code § 6700(a)(19)` supplied m MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT elem (m's `the day`) (supplied's `Good Friday days`) THEN FALSE
        IF m's `seconds after midnight` EQUALS 54000
            THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6700(a)(19) makes Good Friday a holiday from 12 noon until 3 p.m. and does not say whether the instant of 3 p.m. is inside"
        OTHERWISE m's `seconds after midnight` AT LEAST 43200 AND m's `seconds after midnight` LESS THAN 54000

§ `Gov. Code § 6702 to § 6705: Saturdays, closed offices, special holidays`

-- § 6702: "Every Saturday from noon to midnight is a holiday as regards the transaction of business in the public offices of the
-- state and political divisions where laws, ordinances, or charters provide that public offices shall be closed on holidays."
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:43 | 6702. Every Saturday from noon to midnight is a holiday as regards the transaction of business in the public offices of the state and political divisions where laws, ordinances, or charters provide that public offices shall be closed on holidays. This section shall not be construed to prevent or invalidate the issuance, filing, service, execution, or recording of any legal process or written instrument during such period. Public offices of a city shall be closed on those holidays enumerated in Section 6700 unless otherwise provided by charter, ordinance or resolution.
@ref Gov. Code § 6702 (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:43)
GIVEN `laws, ordinances or charters close public offices on holidays` IS A BOOLEAN
      m IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the moment falls in the Saturday holiday of Gov. Code § 6702` `laws, ordinances or charters close public offices on holidays` m MEANS
        `laws, ordinances or charters close public offices on holidays`
    AND `is a Saturday` (m's `the day`)
    AND m's `seconds after midnight` AT LEAST 43200

-- § 6702, second sentence: the section does not prevent "the issuance, filing, service, execution, or recording of any legal process or
-- written instrument during such period".
@ref Gov. Code § 6702 (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:43)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`legal process may be issued, filed, served, executed or recorded in the Saturday holiday of Gov. Code § 6702` MEANS TRUE

-- § 6702, third sentence: "Public offices of a city shall be closed on those holidays enumerated in Section 6700 unless otherwise provided by
-- charter, ordinance or resolution."  The holidays "enumerated in Section 6700" are read as the days of § 6700 that apply to a city under
-- (a)(20)(B), without the Mondays and Fridays that § 6701 adds (fork F-6702city in NOTES).  What a charter, ordinance or resolution
-- provides instead is not in the text.
@ref Gov. Code § 6702 (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:43)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a charter, ordinance or resolution provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`public offices of a city are closed on the day under Gov. Code § 6702` supplied `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` `a charter, ordinance or resolution provides otherwise` d MEANS
    IF `a charter, ordinance or resolution provides otherwise`
    THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 6702 closes the public offices of a city on the holidays enumerated in § 6700 unless a charter, ordinance or resolution provides otherwise, and the text does not say what the charter, ordinance or resolution provides"
    ELSE `a holiday enumerated in Gov. Code § 6700 for a city, county or district` supplied `paragraphs (3), (4), (7) and (20) have been made applicable` d

-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:45 | 6703. (a) Public offices of the state, state institutions, and the University of California shall be closed on Admission Day.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:46 | (b) Public offices of the state and state institutions, including, but not limited to, all state agencies and the Legislature, shall be closed on November 11, Veterans Day. If, in a given year, November 11 falls on a Saturday,
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:47 | then public offices of the state and state institutions, including the Legislature, shall be closed on Friday, November 10. If, in a given year, November 11 falls on a Sunday, then public offices of the state and state institutions, including the Legislature, shall be closed on Monday, November 12. It is the intent of the Legislature that the University of California also be closed on the Veterans Day holiday.
@ref Gov. Code § 6703 (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:45-47)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 6703 requires public offices of the state to be closed on the day` d MEANS
        `the date is the given day of the given month` d 9 9
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 11 11
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 5 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d PLUS 1) 11 11)
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 1 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d MINUS 1) 11 11 AND `is a Sunday` (d MINUS 1))

-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:49 | 6704. The legislative body of any city or district may, by ordinance or resolution, provide that every Saturday is a holiday as respects the transaction of business in the public offices of such cities or districts except that provision shall be made for the continuance of essential public services such as police and fire protection.
@ref Gov. Code § 6704 (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:49)
GIVEN `the legislative body has so provided by ordinance or resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Saturday is a holiday for the public offices of a city or district under Gov. Code § 6704` `the legislative body has so provided by ordinance or resolution` d MEANS
    `the legislative body has so provided by ordinance or resolution` AND `is a Saturday` d

-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:51 | 6705. A special or limited holiday is a holiday applying only to a special class or classes of business, or a special class or classes of persons, and not appointed to be generally observed throughout the State by all classes of business and all classes of persons.
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:52 | On any special or limited holiday appointed by the President or Governor, all courts and public offices of the State, any political subdivision, or any city, shall be open and function in their normal and usual manner. All other public functions shall be performed as on days which are not holidays, and all contracts shall be performed and business transacted as usual, except only
-- src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:53 | as to or by the particular class of business or persons expressly limited or restricted by the provisions of the proclamation appointing or declaring such special or limited holiday.
@ref Gov. Code § 6705 (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:51-53)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`courts and public offices are open on a special or limited holiday appointed by the President or Governor` MEANS TRUE

§ `Civ. Code § 7, § 7.1, § 9: holidays and business days of the Civil Code`

-- Civ. Code § 7: "every Sunday and such other days as are specified or provided for as holidays in the Government Code".  Read here as
-- the day-level holidays of Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701 for the state; the part-day holidays of §§ 6700(a)(19) and 6702 are not days.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:24 | 7. Holidays within the meaning of this code are every Sunday and such other days as are specified or provided for as holidays in the Government Code of the State of California.
@ref Civ. Code § 7 (src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:24)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holiday under Civ. Code § 7` supplied d MEANS
    `is a Sunday` d OR `a holiday under Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701 for the state` supplied d

-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:26 | 7.1. Optional bank holidays within the meaning of Section 9 are:
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:27 | (a) Any closing of a bank because of an extraordinary situation, as that term is defined in the Bank Extraordinary Situation Closing Act (Chapter 20 (commencing with Section 3600) of Division 1 of the Financial Code).
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:28 | (b) Every Saturday.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:29 | (c) Every Sunday.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:30 | (d) January 1st.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:31 | (e) The third Monday in January, known as “Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr. Day.”
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:32 | (f) February 12, known as “Lincoln Day.”
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:33 | (g) The third Monday in February.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:34 | (h) The last Monday in May.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:35 | (i) July 4th.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:36 | (j) The first Monday in September.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:37 | (k) September 9th, known as “Admission Day.”
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:38 | (l) The second Monday in October, known as “Columbus Day.”
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:39 | (m) November 11th, known as “Veteran’s Day.”
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:40 | (n) December 25th.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:41 | (o) Good Friday from 12 noon until closing.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:42 | (p) The Thursday in November appointed as “Thanksgiving Day.”
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:43 | (q) Any Monday following any Sunday on which January 1st, February 12th, July 4th, September 9th, November 11th, or December 25th falls.
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:44 | (r) Any Friday preceding any Saturday on which July 4th, September 9th, or December 25th falls.
@ref Civ. Code § 7.1 (src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:26-44)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an optional bank holiday under Civ. Code § 7.1` supplied d MEANS
        elem d (supplied's `bank closings under the Bank Extraordinary Situation Closing Act`)
    OR  `is a Saturday` d
    OR  `is a Sunday` d
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 1 1
    OR  `Gov. Code § 6700(a)(3) makes the day a holiday` d
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 2 12
    OR  d EQUALS `the n-th given weekday of a month` 3 1 2 (DATE_YEAR d)
    OR  d EQUALS `the last given weekday of a month` 1 5 (DATE_YEAR d)
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 7 4
    OR  d EQUALS `the n-th given weekday of a month` 1 1 9 (DATE_YEAR d)
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 9 9
    OR  d EQUALS `the n-th given weekday of a month` 2 1 10 (DATE_YEAR d)
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 11 11
    OR  `the date is the given day of the given month` d 12 25
    OR  elem d (supplied's `Thursdays appointed as Thanksgiving Day`)
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 1 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d MINUS 1) 1 1 AND `is a Sunday` (d MINUS 1))
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 1 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d MINUS 1) 2 12 AND `is a Sunday` (d MINUS 1))
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 1 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d MINUS 1) 7 4 AND `is a Sunday` (d MINUS 1))
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 1 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d MINUS 1) 9 9 AND `is a Sunday` (d MINUS 1))
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 1 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d MINUS 1) 11 11 AND `is a Sunday` (d MINUS 1))
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 1 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d MINUS 1) 12 25 AND `is a Sunday` (d MINUS 1))
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 5 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d PLUS 1) 7 4 AND `is a Saturday` (d PLUS 1))
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 5 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d PLUS 1) 9 9 AND `is a Saturday` (d PLUS 1))
    OR  (`Weekday of` d EQUALS 5 AND `the date is the given day of the given month` (d PLUS 1) 12 25 AND `is a Saturday` (d PLUS 1))

-- § 7.1(o): Good Friday "from 12 noon until closing".  The closing time of the bank is an input.
@ref Civ. Code § 7.1 (src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:26-44)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      `the bank closes at second` IS A NUMBER
      m IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the moment falls in the Good Friday optional bank holiday of Civ. Code § 7.1(o)` supplied `the bank closes at second` m MEANS
        elem (m's `the day`) (supplied's `Good Friday days`)
    AND m's `seconds after midnight` AT LEAST 43200
    AND m's `seconds after midnight` LESS THAN `the bank closes at second`

-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:46 | 9. All other days than those mentioned in Section 7 are business days for all purposes; provided, that as to any act appointed by law or contract, or in any other way, to be performed by, at, or through any bank organized under the laws of or doing business in this state, any optional bank holiday as defined in Section 7.1 is not a business day; and provided, that any act appointed by law or contract, or in any other way, to be performed on any day which is an optional bank holiday as defined in Section 7.1, by, at, or through any bank or branch or office thereof, whether
-- src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:47 | acting in its own behalf or in any other capacity whatsoever, may be performed on that optional bank holiday if the bank or branch or office by, at, or through which the act is to be performed is open for the transaction of business on that optional bank holiday, or, at the option of the person obligated to perform the act, it may be performed on the next succeeding business day.
@ref Civ. Code § 9 (src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:46-47)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a business day under Civ. Code § 9` supplied d MEANS
    NOT `a holiday under Civ. Code § 7` supplied d

-- § 9, first proviso: for an act "to be performed by, at, or through any bank", an optional bank holiday is not a business day.
@ref Civ. Code § 9 (src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:46-47)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a business day under Civ. Code § 9 for an act to be performed through a bank` supplied d MEANS
    (NOT `a holiday under Civ. Code § 7` supplied d) AND (NOT `an optional bank holiday under Civ. Code § 7.1` supplied d)

-- § 9, second proviso: an act appointed for an optional bank holiday "may be performed on that optional bank holiday if the bank or
-- branch or office ... is open for the transaction of business on that optional bank holiday, or, at the option of the person
-- obligated to perform the act, it may be performed on the next succeeding business day."
@ref Civ. Code § 9 (src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:46-47)
GIVEN `the bank, branch or office is open for business on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an act appointed for an optional bank holiday may be performed on that day itself` `the bank, branch or office is open for business on the day` MEANS
    `the bank, branch or office is open for business on the day`

@ref Civ. Code § 9 (src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:46-47)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next business day after an optional bank holiday on which an act was appointed for a bank` supplied d MEANS
    `the next business day after` d `under the business days` (GIVEN x YIELD `a business day under Civ. Code § 9 for an act to be performed through a bank` supplied x)

§ `Code Civ. Proc. § 10, § 12, § 12a, § 12b: holidays of the Code of Civil Procedure`

-- § 12b: "If any city, county, state, or public office, other than a branch office, is closed for the whole of any day, insofar as the
-- business of that office is concerned, that day shall be considered as a holiday for the purposes of computing time under Sections
-- 12 and 12a."  The caller supplies the days a public office is closed; Gov. Code § 6703 requires the offices of the state to be
-- closed on some days, and those count too.
-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:40 | 12b. If any city, county, state, or public office, other than a branch office, is closed for the whole of any day, insofar as the business of that office is concerned, that day shall be considered as a holiday for the purposes of computing time under Sections 12 and 12a.
@ref Code Civ. Proc. § 12b, Gov. Code § 6703 (src:CCP-ss-1-34:40, src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:45-47)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day is a closure day under Code Civ. Proc. § 12b` supplied d MEANS
    elem d (supplied's `days a public office is closed for the whole day`) OR `Gov. Code § 6703 requires public offices of the state to be closed on the day` d

-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:30 | 10. Holidays within the meaning of this code are every Sunday and any other days that are specified or provided for as judicial holidays in Section 135.
@ref Code Civ. Proc. § 10 (src:CCP-ss-1-34:30)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holiday under Code Civ. Proc. § 10` supplied d MEANS
    `is a Sunday` d OR elem d (supplied's `judicial holidays specified in Code Civ. Proc. section 135`)

-- § 12: "unless the last day is a holiday, and then it is also excluded": the § 10 holidays and, by § 12b, the closure days.
-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:34 | 12. The time in which any act provided by law is to be done is computed by excluding the first day, and including the last, unless the last day is a holiday, and then it is also excluded.
@ref Code Civ. Proc. § 12, § 10, § 12b (src:CCP-ss-1-34:34, src:CCP-ss-1-34:30, src:CCP-ss-1-34:40)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holiday for computing time under Code Civ. Proc. § 12` supplied d MEANS
    `a holiday under Code Civ. Proc. § 10` supplied d OR `the day is a closure day under Code Civ. Proc. § 12b` supplied d

-- § 12a(a): "For purposes of this section, 'holiday' means all day on Saturdays, all holidays specified in Section 135 and, to the extent
-- provided in Section 12b, all days that by terms of Section 12b are required to be considered as holidays."  Read literally, Sunday
-- is not named, and is a holiday here only if section 135 specifies it (not in the deposited text).
-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:36 | 12a. (a) If the last day for the performance of any act provided or required by law to be performed within a specified period of time is a holiday, then that period is hereby extended to and including the next day that is not a holiday. For purposes of this section, “holiday” means all day on Saturdays, all holidays specified in Section 135 and, to the extent provided in Section 12b, all days that by terms of Section 12b are required to be considered as holidays.
-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:37 | (b) This section
-- src:CCP-ss-1-34:38 | applies to Sections 659, 659a, and 921, and to all other provisions of law providing or requiring an act to be performed on a particular day or within a specified period of time, whether expressed in this or any other code or statute, ordinance, rule, or regulation.
@ref Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a) (src:CCP-ss-1-34:36-38)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holiday for the extension of Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), read literally` supplied d MEANS
        `is a Saturday` d
    OR  elem d (supplied's `judicial holidays specified in Code Civ. Proc. section 135`)
    OR  `the day is a closure day under Code Civ. Proc. § 12b` supplied d

-- The same, reading § 10 into § 12a: § 10 says Sundays are holidays "within the meaning of this code" (fork F-holiday in NOTES).
@ref Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), § 10 (src:CCP-ss-1-34:36-38, src:CCP-ss-1-34:30)
GIVEN supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holiday for the extension of Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), taking in the Sundays of § 10` supplied d MEANS
    `is a Sunday` d OR `a holiday for the extension of Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a), read literally` supplied d

§ `Which holiday list governs`

-- Fork F-governs in NOTES.  Each code says "holidays within the meaning of this code"; Gov. Code § 6700 says "the holidays in this state"
-- without limit.  For the extension of a last day, § 12a(b) says the section applies to every provision of law in any code, statute,
-- ordinance, rule or regulation, so that list is the one for the extension whatever the kind of enactment.
@ref Gov. Code § 6700(a), Civ. Code § 7, Code Civ. Proc. §§ 10, 12a(b) (src:GOV-ss-6700-6736:8-31, src:CIV-ss-1-23.6:24, src:CCP-ss-1-34:30, src:CCP-ss-1-34:36-38)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of enactment`
      supplied IS A `Days supplied by the caller`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day is a holiday within the meaning of a provision of kind` kind supplied d MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a provision of the Civil Code` THEN `a holiday under Civ. Code § 7` supplied d
    WHEN `a provision of the Code of Civil Procedure` THEN `a holiday for computing time under Code Civ. Proc. § 12` supplied d
    WHEN `a provision of the Government Code` THEN `a holiday under Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701 for the state` supplied d
    WHEN `a provision of another State statute` THEN `a holiday under Gov. Code § 6700 and § 6701 for the state` supplied d
    WHEN `an ordinance, rule or regulation` THEN REFUSE "no deposited section says which holiday list governs an ordinance, rule or regulation; Gov. Code § 6700(a) says only 'the holidays in this state', and Gov. Code §§ 6700(a)(20)(B), 6702 and 6704 give cities, counties and districts their own rules for some days"
